--- !u!114 &1887391713
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1887391711}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\n\nChapter 3 \u201C Torii\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CThe foxes are in Australia
    too. Come on, let\u2019s just go through the torii and get something to eat\u201D\r\n\r\nJames
    stood up as he said this, and Maddie reluctantly followed him. It was already
    dark outside. The torii looked impressive from the outside, but once they passed
    through them, there was a slight sense of being enclosed. Since it had become
    dark, everything around them was black, and the vermilion colour was the only
    thing they could see.\r\nThey could still see the stairs fairly well until the
    sun completely disappeared, but after a while, Maddie started using the light
    on her phone to see where she was stepping.\r\n\r\n\u201CWhoa, I can\u2019t see
    where it ends\u201D\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\nMaddie looked up. The endless torii continued
    higher and higher, with the path turning to the left. Because the stairs were
    hidden in the shadows, it almost looked as if the torii were floating.\r\nFor
    several more tens of minutes, the three of them forced their tired legs up the
    stairs. The sound of their clothes rubbing against each other, the occasional
    sound of a toe catching on a step and making someone stumble, the sound of the
    trees swaying in the wind, and their sighs all echoed through the darkness.\r\n\r\n\u201CAccording
    to the guide\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nLiam finally spoke again, but he was already
    out of breath.\r\n\r\n\u201CI think it said that once you see the red torii,
    it\u2019s about another ten minutes to the top\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CWhat?\u201D\r\n\r\nJames
    sat down on the stairs.\r\n\r\n\u201CWe\u2019ve already been walking for more
    than twenty minutes from the entrance. If it\u2019s only ten minutes, shouldn\u2019t
    we be able to see the top by now?\u201D\r\n\r\nHe pointed up the stairs. Sure
    enough, the torii still continued far ahead, and there was no sign of any open
    area. Liam dropped his shoulders and raised his hands as if to say he had no
    idea.\r\n\r\n\u201CMaybe we took the wrong path? We haven\u2019t seen a single
    person from that tour group. Wouldn\u2019t we normally run into people coming
    back down?\u201D\r\n\r\nMaddie had a point. They really hadn\u2019t seen a single
    person since they finished treating her knee and returned to the main path.\r\n\r\n\u201CNo,
    it should be a single path. But yeah, you\u2019re right. If it\u2019s one path,
    we should have seen someone coming back down\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CThen let\u2019s
    do this. We\u2019ll climb for another ten minutes, and if we still haven\u2019t
    reached the top, we\u2019ll give up and go back. They\u2019re probably all at
    that festival\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CYeah, let\u2019s do that. Is that okay with
    you, Maddie?\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CFine\u201D\r\n\r\nThe three continued climbing
    and climbing. Their calves and thighs were screaming in pain. As for Maddie,
    looking up made her feel even more discouraged, so she simply kept her eyes on
    the next step and continued moving her feet.\r\nTen minutes passed.\r\nThey still
    couldn\u2019t see the end. Just like before, the path continued straight ahead
    before turning left.\r\n\r\n\u201CI can\u2019t do this anymore\u201D\r\nLiam
    rarely complained, but this time he sat down on the stairs and lowered his head.
    James let out a long sigh and started making strange noises to release his frustration.\r\n\r\n[Fuunna
    monodakoto. Awarejanou]\r\n\r\n\u201CAAAAAAAAAH!\u201D\r\n\r\nMaddie suddenly
    covered both ears and screamed. Liam and James immediately stood up and braced
    themselves, wondering what had happened.\r\n\r\n[konomamadewa isshou derarenzo,
    kitsune wa ganko jakaranou]\r\n\r\nMaddie kept screaming in panic at the mysterious
    voice whispering beside her ears\u2014or rather, inside her head.\r\n\r\n\u201CSomeone
    is talking inside my head! Someone is\u2014\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CMaddie, calm down.
    Nobody is saying anything\u201D\r\n\r\nThe two of them were frightened by how
    different Maddie was acting from usual.\r\n\r\n\u201CIt\u2019s Japanese! It\u2019s
    saying something in Japanese, but I don\u2019t understand!\u201D\r\n\r\nMaddie
    was crying in fear with her hands still covering her ears.\r\n\u201CIt\u2019s
    okay. Calm down. I can understand it. Tell me what you heard\u201D\r\n\r\nLiam
    gently moved Maddie\u2019s arms away from her head and spoke to her. Maddie nodded,
    her face crumpling as she tried not to cry.\r\n\r\n[omaesanra ga ashiwo tometari
    surukara, hora, kitadewanaika. Nekotachino omukaeja]\r\n\r\n\u201CCat\u2026 it
    said cat\u2026 and it also said something about\u2026 legs\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CI
    can\u2019t understand it from just the words. Tell me the whole sentence\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CMaddie,
    Liam\u2026 c-can you see this?\u201D\r\n\r\nJames looked around himself in a
    circle and said this in a trembling voice.\r\nThen, just as he suddenly gasped,
    his body went limp and he collapsed, falling several steps down. Maddie screamed
    even louder when she saw him. Liam rushed over to James. Thankfully, it seemed
    that he wasn\u2019t injured.\r\n\r\n[shikata arumai, sokono torii no sukimawo
    tootte\u2026]\r\n\r\n\u201CWait!\u201D\r\n\r\nMaddie interrupted the mysterious
    voice and tried to tell Liam what she had heard.\r\n\r\n\u201CSoko no sukma wo
    toori.\u201D\r\n\r\n[shitani yuke]\r\n\r\n\u201CIt said \u2018shita ni yuke\u2019!\u201D\r\n\r\nLiam
    tried to make sense of what Maddie had said. Sukma\u2026? What is that\u2026?
    Oh, sukima. The gap.\r\n\r\n\u201CYou mean we\u2019re supposed to go through
    that gap and go down?\u201D\r\n\r\nThey had no idea what was happening. But it
    was obvious that something strange was happening to both Maddie and James. And
    so was the endless stretch of torii.\r\nLiam carried James on his back. He let
    Maddie go through first, then squeezed his own body into the narrow gap between
    the torii.\r\n\r\n\u201CGuh\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nHe immediately regretted not sending
    James through first. He forced himself through, already expecting to end up covered
    in bruises. He came out with so much momentum that he nearly stumbled, but Maddie
    caught him.\r\n\r\n\u201CWe\u2019re going down. Something is wrong with this
    place\u201D\r\n\r\nLiam let Maddie go first while he carried James down the steep
    slope on his back. The path was unmaintained, with tree branches sticking out
    everywhere. Apart from the light from Maddie\u2019s phone occasionally shining
    behind them as if she was checking what was there, they could see nothing but
    darkness.\r\nAnd yet, from the gaps inside the torii that continued alongside
    them, countless glowing eyes were watching them. They disappeared and appeared
    again, following them over and over.\r\nThe two of them ran as if they were being
    chased. They said nothing to each other as they ran, forgetting their exhaustion.\r\nThen,
    suddenly, the view opened up.\r\nThey were standing at some kind of intersection.\r\n"
